- `action(n1, "start")`: Payload label "start" misrepresents the source instruction to "register your participation for the event."
- `branch(b1, ...)` and `branch(b2, ...)`: Lack corresponding `guard` statements to enforce routing conditions, omitting the explicit source logic "If there is no fee... However, if there is a fee..." and "If it is approved... On the other hand, if the purchase request is rejected...".
- `action(n3, ...)`: Lacks an outgoing precedence edge to an end node, contradicting "Once you have registered a post-seminar request, the process will come to an end."
- `precedence(e1, n8)`: Incorrectly sequences end node `e1` before `action(n8, ...)`, violating source chronology where "you will receive an approved notification... you should then register a post-seminar request" without an intervening termination.
- `action(n8, ...)`: Terminates without connecting to an `end` node, leaving the "approved" path structurally incomplete and breaking init-to-end path mirroring.
- `defines(v1, ...)` and `defines(v2, ...)`: Specify empty ranges `{}`, failing to capture the binary value spaces implied by the source (fee yes/no and approved/rejected outcomes).

Structural Check
- [S1] STC6 failed: End nodes must not have outgoing precedence edges. | Violations: e1 | DSL: end(e1)
- [S2] STC8 failed: Each action node must have exactly one incoming and one outgoing edge. | Node `n3` has in=1 and out=0. | Node `n8` has in=1 and out=0. | DSL: action(n3,"Register post-seminar request"); action(n8,"Register post-seminar request")
- [S3] STC11 failed: Each variable definition must have a valid range with at least two distinct values. | Variable `v1` has an invalid range `[]`. | Variable `v2` has an invalid range `[]`.
- [S4] STC16 failed: Every outgoing edge of XOR/OR branches must have exactly one guard. | XOR/OR edge `b1 -> n3` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b1 -> n4` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b2 -> n6` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b2 -> n7` has 0 guards; exactly one is required.
- [S5] STC20 failed: Every non-end node must have a path to at least one end node. | Violations: n3, n8 | DSL: action(n3,"Register post-seminar request"); action(n8,"Register post-seminar request")